     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Targets for 2022
1.1	The number and types of organisations, institutions and private sector companies that participate in the dialogues, meetings and workshops with the partners in regards to regulatory frameworks

1.2	The number of governments in the region that have instituted legal frameworks for responsible reuse of big data for social impact

1.3	Number of private sector companies in target industries allowing reuse in the region.

1.4	Number of applications and methodology developed and tested at large scale with partners for automatic identification and counting of roofs to monitor SDG1. 
1.5	Number of results of large scale projects published and showcased at national and international forums where national bureaus of statistics are the primary target audience. 

1.6	Number of organizations, institutions and private sector companies form the region that benefit from briefings, brainstorming sessions and workshops conducted by Pulse Lab Kampala on the use of data innovation and big data for the SDGs linked to their mandate. 

1.7	Number and type of presentations delivered in conferences and contributions to reports and knowledge products by Pulse Lab Kampala where participation and contribution serves to advance leveraging big data and analytics techniques for the SDGs. 

1.8	Number of Universities and private sector companies that join the Data Science Africa initiative</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pulse Lab Kampala (PLK) , in collaboration with United Nations Global Pulse (UNGP) New York (which is receiving the support of Hewlett and GIZ) and sometimes partnering with others have supported a number of frameworks these include: 1) the Developing Framework for Ethical Artificial Intelligence (AI) roadmap and the Developing Community-Centric Data Exchanges roadmap for Uganda and Ghana. 2) the report by the National Taskforce on National Strategy on the Fourth Industrial revolution for Uganda 3) joined Smart Africa&#x2019;s new data governance working group that is tasked with developing a continental data governance framework blueprint. 4) joined the AU Artificial intelligence (AI) team developing the AU AI Continental Strategy.

A great number of companies now understand the need to share data for social good, especially through the engagements around the data exchange platform that discuss data governance issues, incentives, and technical capabilities required in the platform. In the next one year, we hope to see continued sharing of data in the data exchange.

The work around the data exchange and the joined Smart Africa&#x2019;s new data governance working group that is tasked with developing a continental data governance framework blueprint, but also other engagements around the data strategy, ethics of AI and AU AI continental strategy will all enable the smooth adoption of big data for official statistics. The role that PLK will play in the UN joint programme will also increase the chances of making this a reality.

Engagements with National statistics offices continue, laying firm ground for adoption of large-scale projects.

During this grant period Pulse Lab Kampala (PLK) worked with other institutions to organize Data Science Africa (DSA) 2022 Arusha, Tanzania event. This event attracted more than 120 participants drawn from academia, private sector, governments, civil society and international organisations including the UN. These are drawn from more than 18 countries in Africa and more than 5 outside Africa.

These events are presentations on leveraging big data and analytics by PLK or its partners.

The number of Universities participating in these events have grown to 40 in total and more than 17 for the private sector.

The local chapter - Data Science Africa Uganda has enabled local Universities in Uganda to have never had a chance of participating in Data Science Africa (DSA) events to participate.

In addition to events of Data Science Africa (DSA), PLK has organized workshops to support the data exchange and ethical AI road map and the data exchange platform in support of the tourism sector.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
